/ The whole page. `book` is the parsed lexicon (build: Lexicon::Book) and `config`
/ is config.yml. md() renders block markdown with @{refs} linked, mdi() one line of it,
/ val() a value in the notation; partial() renders another template; styles / script
/ are inlined (or linked with --link).
/
/ One view at a time: the home view (title and index) unless the URL's #fragment names
/ a view or a term, whose group is then shown with that term's card in view
/ (CSS :target and :has; see style.sass). Printing shows every view.
doctype html
html lang="en"
  head
    meta charset="utf-8"
    meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"
    title = config["title"]
    link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"
    link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;0,6..72,600;1,6..72,400;1,6..72,500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"
    == styles
  body
    .shell
      == partial("nav")
      main.page
        == partial("home")
        - book.views.each do |v|
          - if v.kind == :group
            == partial("group", g: v, family: family(v))
          - else
            == partial("extra", x: v, family: family(v))
    == script
